# Runtime state. Everything the server writes while it runs lives under data/:
# the SQLite store, the live plan the team edits through the UI, survey output,
# and the backups. None of it is source, and the store holds every member token
# in plain text alongside every finding and uploaded file.
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# The operator token, generated on first start. Anyone holding it can read the
# whole case file and spend the Claude quota.
.hunt-token
.env

# Logs are runtime output, and the startup banner prints every team token into
# whichever one the server was redirected to.
*.log

# Hand-made transfer bundles. tools.zip carried terrain/ and tools/ to the
# range as a copy, and went stale the moment either changed. Build it when it
# is needed; do not track a second copy of tracked source.
*.zip

# Mission profiles: terrain, plan seed, roster and briefing for one engagement.
# A network map and a team list are not source, and this repository gets
# pushed. missions/example/ is committed so a fresh clone starts and the tests
# have terrain to read; every real engagement stays on the machine running it.
missions/*
!missions/example/

# One engagement's assertions are that engagement's data. test/mission-<code>
# .test.js asserts facts about a specific profile and skips where the profile
# is absent, so it belongs beside the profile rather than in a shared repo.
test/mission-*.test.js

node_modules/

# Agent tooling. Local settings and caches from Claude Code and its plugins;
# .claude/settings.local.json in particular is per-machine and often holds
# paths from somebody's home directory.
.claude/
.superpowers/

# Editor and OS droppings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
